sweep: seeds 1..20, arena 2 chunks each way, runs stopped at 400 s; dials: head_start_s=1000 lesser_max=0 dark_speed_start=0.9 dark_speed_rise=0
speed model (default):
ref_speed         8.000   the chasers' reference speed, metres per second; every row and dial is a multiple of it
dist_per_km       0.050   share of top speed gained for each kilometre the player has covered
dist_max          0.300   the most the distance can add, as a share of top speed
straight_rate     0.050   share of top speed a chaser gains each second it runs straight at its top speed
straight_max      0.200   the most a straight can add, as a share of top speed
straight_turn     0.300   radians a second: it is running straight while it turns slower than this
run_up_bleed      1.000   share of the run-up lost for every radian it turns
turn_drag         0.200   share of its speed a chaser loses for every radian it turns
corner_floor      1.000   least share of the braking a corner asks for that every chaser does before it (1: it never swings into a wall)
wall_stand        0.000   scale on the seconds a chaser stands after meeting a wall head-on (0: it never stops dead)
brake_scale       1.000   scale on every chaser's braking, metres per second squared (1: the rows and the hunter's dial as they are)
hunter_start_bonus    0.170   added to the hunter's dial at the start of a run, and fading to nothing over hunter_bonus_fade_s: a fresh player's margin
hunter_bonus_fade_s  600.000   seconds over which hunter_start_bonus fades away
stairs_lift       1.000   share of a stairs leg's slope a chaser's step is lifted by (0: a flat step, which stalls at the foot of a steep flight)
corner_floor_speed    0.000   L170 P3: the share of its top speed a corner may not take a chaser below (0: the chase as it is; 0.5 is NextBot's)
slip_rate         0.000   L170 SLIP: per second, how fast a chaser's velocity follows its facing (0: it travels along its facing, as it does; 3 is NextBot's sideways friction)
lead_range        0.000   L170 P1: metres; the hunter plans toward where the player will be, leading by lead_base_s plus its distance (to this many metres) over its speed (0: toward where they were seen)
lead_base_s       0.500   L170 P1: seconds of lead before the distance is added (used only when lead_range is above 0)

